{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true,"title":"Freight Identifier Validator"},"description":"Validate freight identifiers by their public check-digit algorithms: shipping container numbers (ISO 6346), air waybill numbers (IATA modulus-7) and IMO ship numbers. text finds and validates every identifier in a string; value + type validates one (value without type is refused); type \"consignment\" with consignment validates a consignment object. An AWB names its airline only when one record holds the prefix; otherwise airline_candidates[] lists every holder, never a guessed carrier. AWB: airline prefix + the airline from the AWB-prefix dataset when ONE record holds the prefix \u2014 when several do (e.g. 020: Lufthansa and Lufthansa Cargo), airline is null and airline_candidates[] lists every holder with airline_note saying why, never a guessed carrier. For container TYPE specs use container_lookup; for the AWB-prefix dataset airline_lookup. Rate-limited: a limit error carries reset_at, the UTC time the allowance resets. Structural only \u2014 a valid check digit means well-formed, NOT that the container, shipment or vessel exists.","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"consignment":{"additionalProperties":{},"description":"With type \"consignment\": the consignment object to validate.","propertyNames":{"type":"string"},"type":"object"},"text":{"description":"Free text to scan for container / AWB / IMO identifiers. Provide this OR value + type.","type":"string"},"type":{"description":"Type of value: container (ISO 6346), awb, imo; or consignment with the consignment argument.","enum":["container","awb","imo","consignment"],"type":"string"},"value":{"description":"One identifier to validate; requires type.","type":"string"}},"type":"object"},"name":"validate","outputSchema":{"$schema":"http://jso